% SECTION III: SYSTEM MODEL
% =========================================
\section{System Model and Problem Formulation}
\label{sec:system}

We consider a video streaming system where a video is divided into $K$ chunks. For each chunk $k$, the ABR agent selects a bitrate $R_k$ from a discrete set $\mathcal{R}$. The goal is to maximize the Quality of Experience (QoE) defined as:
\begin{equation}
QoE = \sum_{k=1}^{K} \left( q(R_k) - \lambda |q(R_k) - q(R_{k-1})| - \mu T_{stall, k} \right)
\end{equation}
where $q(R_k)$ is the visual quality (VMAF), the second term penalizes quality switching, and $T_{stall, k}$ is the rebuffering time.

\subsection{Lyapunov Optimization for Stability}
To guarantee buffer stability, we formulate the problem as a constrained optimization. Let $B_t$ be the buffer level at time $t$. We define a Lyapunov function $L(B_t) = \frac{1}{2} (B_t - B_{ref})^2$, where $B_{ref}$ is the target buffer level. The Lyapunov drift $\Delta L(B_t)$ measures the deviation from the target.
Our agent minimizes the drift-plus-penalty term:
\begin{equation}
\min \Delta L(B_t) - V \cdot Reward_t
\end{equation}
By incorporating this drift term into the PPO reward function, we force the agent to prioritize buffer stability whenever $B_t$ deviates significantly from $B_{ref}$, ensuring a bounded queue size and minimizing stall probability.

