\section{Experimental Evaluation}
\label{sec:eval}

\subsection{Experimental Setup}
\label{subsec:setup}
\subsubsection{Network Traces and Video Dataset}
We evaluate our proposed method using a diverse set of network traces:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{FCC Broadband Dataset:} Represents stable but variable network conditions.
    \item \textbf{HSDPA (Norway) Dataset:} Highly volatile mobile network traces with sudden drops.
\end{itemize}
For video content, we used the standard DASH dataset (\textit{Big Buck Bunny}, \textit{Sintel}, \textit{Tears of Steel}) encoded at multiple bitrates $\{300, \dots, 4300\}$ kbps with 4s chunks.

\subsubsection{Implementation Details}
The agent is implemented using PyTorch and \textit{Stable-Baselines3}. The network consists of two hidden layers with 64 units each. We trained for 100k episodes with a learning rate of $2.5 \times 10^{-4}$ and entropy coefficient $0.01$.

\subsection{Performance Analysis}
